    {
      "app": "Netflix",
      "caption": "Netflix just updated its policy. Updated July 20, 2026.\n\n- Netflix deleted the line saying it shares your viewing history with advertisers\n- The removal makes data-sharing practices less transparent to users\n- It's unclear if the practice stopped or just the disclosure was removed\n- Ad-supported plan subscribers may still have viewing data shared\n\nRemoving an explicit disclosure about advertiser data-sharing raises transparency concerns, especially for users on Netflix's ad-supported tier.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- Check your Netflix privacy settings and limit ad personalization if possible\n- Review Netflix's full Privacy Statement for current data-sharing details\n- Consider whether the ad-supported plan aligns with your privacy comfort level\n\n#Netflix #privacy #termsofservice #dataprivacy #tosmonitor",
      "detected_at": "2026-08-20T01:27:14.345505+00:00",
