      "app": "Discord",
      "caption": "Discord just updated its policy. Updated July 24, 2026.\n\n- Discord now explicitly states it does NOT store your screen-share content\n- Previous wording was ambiguous; new version clearly separates screen content from thumbnails\n- Thumbnail cover image from your stream is still retained for a short time\n- No new data is collected \u2014 this is a clarification, not an expansion\n\nThis is a wording clarification, not a new data practice. Users gain slightly more transparency about screen-share storage.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- No action needed \u2014 your screen-share content was never stored under old policy either\n- Review Discord's privacy settings if you regularly screen-share sensitive content\n- Follow @tos_monitor to catch any future changes that do expand data collection\n\n#Discord #privacy #termsofservice #dataprivacy #tosmonitor",
