    {
      "app": "Facebook",
      "caption": "Facebook just updated its policy. Effective July 23, 2026.\n\n- Meta AI now uses your interests, location, friends, and partner data to personalize responses\n- New policy section explicitly describes how your profile fuels Meta AI recommendations\n- 'AI at Meta' rebranded to 'Meta AI features' throughout, clarifying scope of data use\n- Large sections of explanatory annotations removed, making the policy shorter but less detailed\n\nA new explicit section confirms your full profile\u2014interests, location, third-party data\u2014is used to personalize Meta AI. Users should know this.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- Review your Meta AI data settings at facebook.com/privacy/genai\n- Check Ad Preferences and limit data used for personalization in Accounts Center\n- Use 'Your activity off Meta technologies' tool to restrict third-party data sharing\n\n#Facebook #privacy #termsofservice #dataprivacy #tosmonitor",
      "detected_at": "2026-08-20T01:27:14.346532+00:00",
