    {
      "app": "Instagram",
      "caption": "Instagram just updated its policy. Updated July 28, 2026.\n\n- Automated scraping now governed by a formal 'Automated Data Collection Terms' document\n- Instagram can revoke permission for any automated data collection at any time\n- Bots and scrapers must comply with the new terms even if previously allowed\n- Clarifies that automated access rules apply whether or not you're logged in\n\nThis formalises and expands restrictions on scraping and bots, and gives Instagram broader power to revoke access without notice.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- If you use any automation tools on Instagram, review the new Automated Data Collection Terms\n- Developers or businesses using the API should audit their current data practices now\n- Regular users: no action needed, but know Instagram is cracking down on scrapers\n\n#Instagram #privacy #termsofservice #dataprivacy #tosmonitor",
