      "caption": "Twitch updated its Privacy Notice on August 12, 2026, and added new language explicitly allowing your data to be used for machine learning and artificial intelligence development, including training generative AI models across Twitch and Amazon's products and services. Previously, the policy described data use for recommendations, advertising, and general service improvement. Now it goes further, stating Twitch may use data to develop or deploy generative AI. Because Twitch is an Amazon subsidiary, this extends your data's reach into Amazon's broader AI ecosystem. No opt-out mechanism is mentioned in this update. You should visit Twitch's Privacy Choices page and review Amazon's Generative AI Development Disclosure to understand your current options.\n\n#Twitch #amazon #privacypolicy #aitraining #generativeai #dataprivacy #streamers #userdata",
