      "app": "Amazon",
      "caption": "Amazon updated its Conditions of Use on August 14, 2026, replacing a straightforward court-dispute clause with a detailed mandatory arbitration system. Under the new terms, if you have a complaint about Amazon \u2014 a bad charge, a faulty product, a policy dispute \u2014 you can no longer take it to a regular court with a judge or jury. Instead, you must first contact customer service and negotiate for up to 60 days, then go through a JAMS arbitration process. A new class-action waiver means you cannot join other customers in a lawsuit against Amazon; each person must fight their case alone. The only notable carve-out is for personal injury or property damage from a product, which will now be governed by the law of the state where the harm occurred....\n\n#Amazon #arbitration #consumerrights #termsofservice #privacyrights #classaction #onlineshopping #toschange",
