      "app": "Robinhood",
      "caption": "Robinhood updated its privacy policy on August 18, 2026, with changes focused on artificial intelligence agents. The policy now explicitly states that Robinhood collects your usage data whether you access the app directly or through an external AI agent acting on your behalf. It also names third-party AI agents alongside Google and Apple as services that can connect to your account and send Robinhood your profile information. This matters because an AI agent operating on your account could generate data Robinhood collects and potentially uses to train its own AI features. If you use or plan to use any AI tool that links to Robinhood, review the updated Customer Agreement and check which services have access to your account.\n\n#Robinhood #privacypolicy #AIagents #fintech #dataprivacy #agenticAI #investingapp #tosmonitor",
